# MagiskPolicy statements use space-separated class names; `self:bpf` is not
# valid here and silently left dae without these grants. Magisk already grants
# most of them, but keep the rule explicit for policy changes.
# Note: pname routing additionally needs dae's cgroup sock_create hook. On
# ROMs where netd's cgroupsock_inet already owns that cgroup attach type, the
# kernel rejects the second attach and no SELinux rule can change that.
allow magisk magisk bpf { map_create map_read map_write prog_load prog_run }
